{"created": "2024-02-13T08:34:45.114366+00:00", "modified": "2024-02-13T08:34:45.437367+00:00", "id": 10652994, "conceptrecid": "8065874", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.8065874", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "metadata": {"title": "Python scripts to test gravity with the dynamics of wide binary stars", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "publication_date": "2024-02-13", "description": "<p>This is version 5 to provide supplementary codes for arXiv:2402.05720.</p>\n<p>It also updates the existing codes from the previous versions.</p>\n<p>This version should replace the relevant previous versions.</p>\n<p>In using `run_wb_v5.py' (an updated code)&nbsp; and&nbsp; `run_vtilde_wb_v5.py' (a new code), scatters of proper motions can be allowed in the Monte Carlo (MC) draw of probabilities of accelerations or normalized velocities. In other words, each MC can take values from normal probability functions rather than the reported most likely values of proper motions in calculating accelerations and normalized velocities. When the sample is less strictly selected as in the `Chae (2023a) sample', tests with simulated data show that alowing scatters can bias the results somewhat. However, in strictly selected samples such as the `pure binary sample' of Chae (2024) or the `new sample' of arXiv:2402.05720 it makes negligible difference to allow scatters or not. The default choice is not to allow the scatters. However, the user can choose either option through the parameter `pm_scatter'.</p>\n<p>Required input files (other than one file being uploaded) can be accessed from the previous versions.</p>\n<p>Questions can be directed to kyuhyunchae@gmail.com or chae@sejong.ac.kr.</p>\n<p>Last updated 2024-02-13.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Chae, Kyu-Hyun", "affiliation": "Sejong University", "orcid": "0000-0002-6016-2736"}], "keywords": ["dynamics of wide binary stars", "GAIA DR3", "modified Newtonian dynamics", "modified gravity"], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 4, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "8065874"}}]}, "notes": "<p>Chae, K.-H. 2023, Astrophysical Journal, 952, 128</p>\n<p>Chae, K.-H., 2024, Astrophysical Journal, 960, 114</p>\n<p>Chae, K.-H. 2024, arXiv:2402:05720 (submitted to ApJ)</p>"}, "title": "Python scripts to test gravity with the dynamics of wide binary stars", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10652994", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10652994?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10652994", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/8065874", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/8065874", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8065874", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.8065874", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10652994/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10652994/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10652994/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10652994/access/grants", 